<title>RUSSIA: Russian Uralsvyazinform 1996 IAS EPS 11.68 RBLS.</title>
<headline>Russian Uralsvyazinform 1996 IAS EPS 11.68 RBLS.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian regional telecommunications company AO Uralsvyazinform said on Wednesday its 1996 earning per share ratio rose to 11.68 roubles from 5.54 roubles in 1995 to international accounting standards.</p>
<p>Year ended December 31:</p>
<p>				     1996		 1995</p>
<p>    Revenues		    726.08	     575.63</p>
<p>    Costs			(539.49)	   (418.22)</p>
<p>    Earnings		    186.59	     157.41</p>
<p>Net profit/loss from</p>
<p>    financial investment     (2.30)	     (4.52)</p>
<p>Net interest and</p>
<p>    similar payments	  (39.04)	    (44.34)</p>
<p>Profit from foreign</p>
<p>    exchange operations	 2.57		 0.74</p>
<p>    Net profit before tax   147.82	     109.30</p>
<p>    Profit tax		  (41.23)	    (58.75)</p>
<p>    Net profit after tax    106.59		50.55</p>
<p>    Dividend payments	  (5.93)	     (3.55)</p>
<p>    Retained profit	   100.67		47.00</p>
<p>    EPS			    11.68 rbls	  5.54 rbls</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billion roubles, unless otherwise specified. Face value of a share is 100 roubles. The company is located in Perm in the Urals. Coopers &amp; Lybrand audited the figures.</p>
<p>($=5,776 roubles)</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
